You’re chaining through several calls without any null checks. `user`, `user.getProfile()`, `user.getProfile().getName()`, or `trim()` on a null could all cause an NPE.

A simple defensive fix:

```java
public String getUserName(User user) {
    if (user == null) return null;

    Profile profile = user.getProfile();
    if (profile == null) return null;

    String name = profile.getName();
    if (name == null) return null;

    return name.trim();
}
```

Or, if you want a default instead of `null`:

```java
return name == null ? "" : name.trim();
```

You should also investigate which value is actually null (e.g., with a debugger or logging) and fix it closer to the source if possible.

